is\nforecast.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...St Johns River near Deland.\n\n* WHEN...Until Thursday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 4.0 feet, Docks and piers are completely submerged at\nPier 44 Marina. Many docks are partially submerged at Hontoon\nLanding Marina.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 8:30 AM EDT Wednesday the stage was 4.0 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 3.5 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise to a crest of 4.0 feet\nthe next couple days. It will then fall below flood stage late in\nthe week.\n- Flood stage is 4.0 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Motorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued late tonight at 1215 AM EDT.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSMLB"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS82 KMLB 281303"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING NOW IN EFFECT UNTIL THURSDAY EVENING"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.EXT.KMLB.FL.W.0004.000000T0000Z-261030T0000Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-10-29T20:00:00-04:00"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.32a6624b03ca4bdc3923c468120fbeec7a6da027.001.1,2026-10-27T10:04:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a018ff21889eafe6543a9dc3086e3eeb8943dea8.001.1,2026-10-26T21:41:00-04:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["FLS"],"NationalWeatherService":["FLW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.38b2fe4c99aae628ba1f3929976442500b6b4e68.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-94.97,45.02],[-94.89,45.18],[-94.76,45.06],[-94.76,45.04],[-94.92,44.98],[-94.97,45.02]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.38b2fe4c